    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the street in both directions.\n• Post the secondary access point location on any Knox Box or exterior key lockbox so responders can locate it quickly on arrival.\n• Keep the large paved area clear of parked vehicles along at least one full side to provide an unobstructed staging area for emergency equipment.\n• Mark or label the detached structure on any posted site map near the front entrance so responders know a second structure is on the property.\n• Clear a walking path between the main residence and the detached structure wide enough for two people to pass with equipment.\n• Trim any landscaping along the walkway that narrows passage or reduces visibility between the residence and detached structure.\n• Post a simple site diagram at the front of the property showing the location of the main residence, detached structure, patio, and all access points.\n• Identify the rear access limitation to responding units by posting a sign or notation at the front indicating \"No rear vehicle access\" so crews do not commit equipment to a restricted route.\n• Keep any gate or opening that connects the paved area to the rear of the property unlocked or secured with a combination accessible to emergency responders."
